    "narrative": "For July 11, 2026, **Vinnie Pasquantino** (76.21) and **Seiya Suzuki** (73.90) headline our daily efficiency projections as the clear must-starts. **Vinnie Pasquantino** benefits from a massive 16% park adjustment and a favorable matchup against the right-handed Kyle Bradish, while **Seiya Suzuki** is buoyed by elite BvP metrics\u2014a 25 plate appearance sample size providing an 8% boost\u2014and a significant SP skill advantage against the lefty Nick Lodolo. **Mickey Moniak** (72.29) remains a high-floor play in the #2 hole; despite minor park penalties, his platoon advantage against Tyler Mahle makes him a locked-in core piece for today\u2019s production.\n\nRisk management remains a primary focus, particularly with the 39% rain threat hanging over **Edwin Arroyo** and **Seiya Suzuki**. While **Seiya Suzuki** possesses a high enough efficiency score to weather the risk, **Edwin Arroyo** sits in the marginal tier (53.25); any weather-related delay could quickly dampen his value. Our closest bench call was **Austin Riley** (53.21), who fell just shy of the UTIL slot occupied by **Josh Naylor** (53.42). While **Austin Riley** profiles well against Matthew Liberatore, the combination of a poor wind forecast and a projected bottom-third batting order kept him on the pine. Meanwhile, we are exercising caution with **Corbin Carroll** (59.02); despite his elite speed, the matchup against Yoshinobu Yamamoto and the catcher's high-efficiency pop time forces a downward adjustment to his baseline, though his talent remains too high to bench in a category-scarcity environment.",
